  "description": "BA-86 code review item 1 (BLOCKER) live proof: POST /datasets/:name/model/query against a real World Cup Postgres datasource via the CLI (node dist/cli.js --port 3100 --data-dir /tmp/qti-ba86 --no-open). Proves compile-sql.ts's quoteTableRef fix: the 'world_cup.world_cup.matches' binding key compiles to FROM \"world_cup\".\"matches\" (catalog segment dropped, schema.table quoted per-segment) and Postgres accepts it directly -- the pre-fix bug quoted the whole dotted key as one identifier (FROM \"world_cup.world_cup.matches\"), which Postgres rejected as an unknown relation.",
